1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:07,464
NARRATOR: Weeks later, Cartman was the star of every emotional assembly. Or so he believed.

2
00:00:07,814 --> 00:00:08,915
CARTMAN: You're welcome, everybody.

3
00:00:09,415 --> 00:00:11,814
CARTMAN: So, feelings. What's the deal with feelings, am I right?

4
00:00:12,114 --> 00:00:14,114
[Crickets]

5
00:00:14,114 --> 00:00:14,957
CARTMAN: Feelings? Anyone?

6
00:00:15,157 --> 00:00:16,157
[Somebody coughs]

7
00:00:16,557 --> 00:00:21,257
CARTMAN (thinking): Oh no. Oh no, no, no. It's not landing. My humor isn't working on this crowd.

8
00:00:21,557 --> 00:00:25,304
CARTMAN (thinking): And these two dweebs can't save me. They aren't funny either. I'm doomed!

9
00:00:25,904 --> 00:00:26,465
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Now?

10
00:00:26,615 --> 00:00:27,102
PC PRINCIPAL: Now.

11
00:00:28,002 --> 00:00:29,720
PC PRINCIPAL: Chad. The five stages of grief.

12
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:31,994
EMOTIONAL CHAD: After dropping your phone in the toilet.

13
00:00:32,544 --> 00:00:33,686
PC PRINCIPAL: Stage one: Denial.

14
00:00:33,886 --> 00:00:36,973
EMOTIONAL CHAD: That's not my phone. My phone is in my pocket.

15
00:00:37,673 --> 00:00:38,731
PC PRINCIPAL: Stage two: Anger.

16
00:00:38,931 --> 00:00:41,109
EMOTIONAL CHAD: WHO DESIGNED A TOILET THIS PHONE-SHAPED?!

17
00:00:41,659 --> 00:00:42,934
PC PRINCIPAL: Stage three: Bargaining.

18
00:00:43,134 --> 00:00:46,934
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Rice. I'll put it in rice. I'll put my whole life in rice.

19
00:00:47,484 --> 00:00:48,765
PC PRINCIPAL: Stage four: Depression.

20
00:00:49,365 --> 00:00:52,134
EMOTIONAL CHAD: I'll never see my four thousand screenshots again.

21
00:00:52,684 --> 00:00:54,151
PC PRINCIPAL: Stage five: Acceptance.

22
00:00:54,951 --> 00:00:56,570
EMOTIONAL CHAD: I'm a landline guy now.

23
00:00:56,670 --> 00:00:58,470
[The crowd goes wild]

24
00:00:58,470 --> 00:01:02,822
EMOTIONAL CHAD: We've always been funny, bro. We were toning it down so you could shine.

25
00:01:03,022 --> 00:01:04,486
PC PRINCIPAL: Bringing you up was the whole point.

26
00:01:04,986 --> 00:01:08,485
CARTMAN: You were FUNNY this whole time?! You TRICKED me! You let me think you were dweebs!

27
00:01:08,685 --> 00:01:10,056
PC PRINCIPAL: Dude, it wasn't a trick, it was-

28
00:01:10,056 --> 00:01:12,565
CARTMAN: I don't need you! I'll do my own show! A SOLO show!

29
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:15,465
[Laughter]

30
00:01:14,265 --> 00:01:15,405
CARTMAN: Thank you! I'm here all week!

31
00:01:15,605 --> 00:01:18,557
NARRATOR: The solo shows went all right. He got laughs.

32
00:01:18,907 --> 00:01:26,675
NARRATOR: But for some reason he couldn't explain, it felt a little empty. Not nearly as fun as showing those two dweebs how cool he was.

33
00:01:27,025 --> 00:01:29,561
CARTMAN (thinking): They're laughing. So why does this feel so... meh?

34
00:01:30,461 --> 00:01:33,620
CARTMAN (thinking): That's it. I quit. Comedy is stupid. Everything is stupid.

35
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:36,120
[The principal's door is open a crack]

36
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:38,167
CARTMAN (thinking): Oh great. Here it comes.

37
00:01:38,467 --> 00:01:40,067
[What Cartman imagines]

38
00:01:38,667 --> 00:01:40,455
PC PRINCIPAL: Well, well, well. Look who's crawling back.

39
00:01:40,655 --> 00:01:42,625
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Crawling back like a little slug, huh?

40
00:01:42,825 --> 00:01:43,339
CARTMAN: Squish.

41
00:01:43,539 --> 00:01:44,878
EMOTIONAL CHAD: CARTMAN! Bro! You came!

42
00:01:45,078 --> 00:01:47,380
PC PRINCIPAL: Dude! We caught your solo show. Real chops.

43
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:48,786
CARTMAN: You're not going to rub it in?

44
00:01:48,986 --> 00:01:51,717
PC PRINCIPAL: Rub what in? It's not about winning or losing, dude.

45
00:01:51,917 --> 00:01:56,281
EMOTIONAL CHAD: We just want to have fun with you. And we want you to be as great as you can be.

46
00:01:56,481 --> 00:01:58,054
CARTMAN: Even if I roast you? On stage?

47
00:01:58,954 --> 00:02:00,396
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Bro. Please roast us.

48
00:02:00,596 --> 00:02:02,613
PC PRINCIPAL: It makes the show more fun for everybody.

49
00:02:02,813 --> 00:02:03,260
CARTMAN: Deal.

50
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:11,271
CARTMAN: PC Principal wears sunglasses indoors because underneath, he has the most caring eyes you've ever seen. It's disgusting.

51
00:02:12,671 --> 00:02:16,941
CARTMAN: And Chad cried at a protein bar commercial. Twice. It was the same commercial.

52
00:02:17,541 --> 00:02:18,599
EMOTIONAL CHAD: It was beautiful.

53
00:02:19,699 --> 00:02:21,146
HECKLER: Yeah! They're total freaks!

54
00:02:21,346 --> 00:02:22,074
HECKLER: LOSERS!

55
00:02:22,274 --> 00:02:24,174
[A few kids snicker. It feels off.]

56
00:02:23,374 --> 00:02:25,974
[The bros don't defend themselves. They look at Cartman.]

57
00:02:25,474 --> 00:02:28,028
CARTMAN (thinking): Losers. Huh. That sounded a lot worse from out here.

58
00:02:28,328 --> 00:02:30,206
CARTMAN (thinking): That's not roasting. That's just mean.

59
00:02:30,806 --> 00:02:32,905
HECKLER: Did you see their faces? Total freaks.

60
00:02:33,206 --> 00:02:34,881
CARTMAN: Hey. Those two? They're my co-hosts.

61
00:02:35,081 --> 00:02:38,311
CARTMAN: I get to roast them, because they're in on it. That's called comedy.

62
00:02:38,511 --> 00:02:39,995
CARTMAN: What you did is called being a jerk.

63
00:02:40,195 --> 00:02:42,205
HECKLER: Dude, you call them dweebs all the time.

64
00:02:42,405 --> 00:02:43,589
CARTMAN: Yeah. MY dweebs. Back off.

65
00:02:44,089 --> 00:02:47,029
CARTMAN: Trust me. I've been where you are. Mess around, and you'll find out.

66
00:02:49,230 --> 00:02:51,230
[Down the hall, the bros saw everything]

67
00:02:50,030 --> 00:02:51,190
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Good job, bro.

68
00:02:51,290 --> 00:02:52,196
PC PRINCIPAL: Good job, bro.

69
00:02:52,696 --> 00:02:56,140
NARRATOR: And somewhere along the way, Eric Cartman stopped being bored.
